::::section {#components}
## Custom Components

:::legal-clause {#legal-it jurisdiction="IT" fallback="children"}
The `legal-clause` component renders as ordinary text when unsupported. The
component manifest can add schema and rendering hints without changing the
fallback semantics.
:::

:::approval-card {#approval release="{{vars.release}}" status="pending" fallback="children"}
Approval is pending security review. Agents must create a change record
through the Agent SDK before modifying this block.
:::

:::agent-review {#agent-findings sensitivity="internal" fallback="children"}
- [x] Stable IDs on critical sections
- [x] Unknown components preserve children
- [x] Manifest digests verified at package open
- [ ] Trust policy bound at host integration time
:::
::::

::::section {#i18n}
## Internationalisation

NODX 1.0 propagates `lang` and `dir` from front matter and inline spans:

- Latin: The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.
- [Arabic]{lang="ar" dir="rtl"} (right-to-left): [٩٨ ريال — استعراض]{lang="ar" dir="rtl"}
- [Chinese]{lang="zh-Hans"}: 国际化展示。
- [Hebrew]{lang="he" dir="rtl"} (block-level fallback in body): שלום.

Inline switches keep the surrounding paragraph LTR while marking the run with
`lang`, `dir`, and `title` attributes — the renderer emits matching HTML.
::::

